@flavorjones this looks really good! Nothing jumps out at me as missing (aside from the subsequent steps still to do, that you noted above).

One slightly odd thing about Fizzy's schema is there are some model references in a JSON field on the Event model. It shouldn't matter in this case since none of the IDs are changing; I'm just mentioning it because it's a little hidden.

For the attachment URLs, those will show up at `https://fizzy.37signals.com/u/{whatever}` in the markdown bodies. So I think if you generally update the subdomain in that text, it should take care of that.

@jzimdars I think I fixed the bulk of the performance issue but need to deploy to staging to confirm, and I was having trouble doing that (I'm handling that with @kevinmcconnell).

I'll start the refactoring in a separate branch. I started with it directly, but I don't want to delay the testing/validation we want to do. I think there is some good cleanup to do, and I think it is a good task for me to do next as I get familiar with everything.

We should definitely add pagination, at least, to the "recently closed" list, so I'll add that as part of the refactor.

@Kevin thanks for the suggestions. A problem I see with not making notifications notifiable is that it would be hard to handle the case where you edit a comment to add a notification after creating the comment, or a card, which is relatively common. 
You are adding a new mention that way, but there is no new notification right now.

I think it makes sense to get mentions notify when they are created. You are right that we need to remove the notification overlap, I'll see how to do that and to think about the whole thing a bit more. To me, making mentions a notfiable unit makes sense from a semantics perspective, instead of using them as some data point when representing notifications.

@jorgemanrubia thanks for reviewing. I added a helper method for rendering a new template for `events` with `type: card` that have the `card_published` action so we can render an excerpt and attachments for when a new card is published. It replaces that awkward check in the `layout` partial

I also extracted a shared partial for the attachments rendering between the two. 

Would you take another look?

